    qemu-ipccall-direct-x86_64-smp-request-smoke: remove an empty if-block
    
    The script has carried an empty `if (( ! fail )); then` / `fi` block
    since it was added (15114160), which bash rejects as a syntax error at
    line 67. So the only live cell that grades IPCCALL_DIRECT_SMP_SERVER_BLOCKED
    (the x86_64 SMP oracle whose fact collection SCHED-LOCK2A gates) could not
    run on the baseline. The block did nothing; removing it is the whole
    repair.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLpmtT4bLN2gX3DCKAXYp8

